    "title": "Reporting Opinions and Disagreements Formally",
    "title_ko": "격식체 의견 불일치 표현",
    "focus_axis": "grammar"
  },
  "context": {
    "explanation_en": "Formal ways to disagree soften the impact: 'I see your point, but ...', 'With respect, I have to disagree', 'I'm not entirely convinced that ...'. These maintain politeness while still expressing a different opinion clearly.",
    "explanation_ko": "격식체로 반대할 때는 충격을 완화하는 표현을 씁니다: 'I see your point, but ...', 'With respect, I have to disagree', 'I'm not entirely convinced that ...'. 정중함을 유지하면서도 다른 의견을 명확히 표현합니다.",
    "key_expressions": [
      {
        "en": "With respect, I have to disagree.",
        "ko": "죄송하지만 저는 동의할 수 없어요."
      },
      {
        "en": "I'm not entirely convinced that this will work.",
        "ko": "이게 효과가 있을지 완전히 확신이 서지는 않아요."
      },
      {
        "en": "I see your point, but I think there's another way to look at it.",
        "ko": "이해는 하지만, 다르게 볼 수도 있다고 생각해요."
      }
    ]
  },
